        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ba773d2d-785c-5b7e-9535-90c0fbb14ea6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Canals: Sandy and Beaver Canal, Morris Canal\n- Places: Bolivar, Ohio; Glasgow, Pennsylvania; Easton, Pennsylvania; Phillipsburg, New Jersey; Newark; Jersey City; New York Harbor; Ohio River; Ohio and Erie Canal; Delaware River\n\nFacts:\n- The Sandy and Beaver Canal ran 73 miles from the Ohio and Erie Canal at Bolivar, Ohio, to the Ohio River at Glasgow, Pennsylvania.\n- The Morris Canal operated from 1829 to 1924 as a 107-mile common carrier coal canal across northern New Jersey in the United States.\n- The Morris Canal connected industrial canals at Easton, Pennsylvania, across the Delaware River from Phillipsburg, New Jersey, to New York Harbor and New York City markets through terminals in Newark and Jersey City, New Jersey.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d547b12d-ba3b-59d0-8e5b-9daa1feceec9",
